            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did bahu mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आतिथ्यम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आतिथ्यम् (ātithyam) — \"hospitality\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आतिथ्यम् (ātithyam) is hospitality: not the guest, but everything owed to one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The अतिथिः you already know is stretched into the treatment that guest receives, so the word names a duty rather than a person."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Classically it runs in an order, and you have the words for all of it: an आसनम् first, then पानीयम्, then अन्नम्. आतिथ्यम् (ātithyam) is that whole sequence in one word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The guest word, turned into what is owed to the guest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
