        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: विनयः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विनयः (vinayaḥ) — \"good conduct, training\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विनयः (vinayaḥ) is the bearing of someone well brought up — modest, disciplined, easy to be near."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its pieces are vi-, \"away, apart\", and the leading doing-word नयति: to have विनयः (vinayaḥ) is to have been led away from what was rough in you. Training and good manners are one word here, because the second is thought to come out of the first."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Buddhist books of monastic training carry this word as their name."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Manners understood as training rather than as polish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
