          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: विश्वासः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विश्वासः (viśvāsaḥ) — \"trust, confidence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विश्वासः (viśvāsaḥ) is trust — and the picture inside it is breathing out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is vi- with śvas, \"to breathe\": to trust someone is to let the breath go, to stop holding it. English says much the same thing when it calls a friend a confidant, from Latin for with faith."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hindi viśvās is unchanged, and viśvāsghāt, a betrayal, is the same word with the breaking of it attached."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Trust, described as the moment you stop holding your breath."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
